# Raw and converted mass spectrometry data. A single Q Exactive RAW file from
# PXD001584 is about 2.6 GiB and there are eighteen of them, so nothing under
# data/ is ever tracked. Committing one of these to git is close to
# unrecoverable, which is why this file is the first commit in the repository.
data/
# The directory is ignored but its README explains the layout and the disk
# arithmetic, so it has to be tracked.
!data/README.md
*.raw
*.RAW
*.mzML
*.mzML.gz
*.mzid
*.pin

# Search engine intermediates that are large and fully regenerable.
*.sage.tsv
fragment_index/

# R session state
.Rproj.user/
.Rhistory
.RData
.Ruserdata
renv/library/
renv/staging/

# BiocFileCache, which R packages populate on first use
.cache/BiocFileCache/
BiocFileCache/

# Conda environment directories, if created inside the project
envs/
.conda/

# Editor and OS noise
*.swp
.DS_Store
__pycache__/

# Regenerable analysis intermediates. The densities table is one row per
# peptide per run per stage and runs to about 10 MB; the QFeatures object is
# a binary blob. Both are rebuilt by differential.R in under a minute, and
# neither is a result anyone would read. The tables that are results, and
# every figure, stay tracked.
results/*_normalisation_densities.tsv
results/*_qfeatures.rds
